  "details": "While we now have text moderation for Bios and Usernames, I think it's about time until it comes for the chatbox. So in the case this really happens, which would be the logical option since as of today chatboxes are used in many malicious ways..\n\nSo, I would like to suggest here, my vision of this integration. \n\nTo keep the right balance between moderation and users free speech, the right way to apply this would be to have the moderation active in public instances such as \"public, group public\", and in privates instances (depending on what is considered \"private\" in the community guidelines) such as \"Invite and Invite+ instances, Friends and Friends+ instances, and Group and Group+ instances\", this moderation should be turned off and let out to the choosing of the moderators of the group instances or to the instances owner in the case of a user private instance.\n\nTL:DR : Chatbox moderation turned on in public but kept off in private instances.\n\nExcuse me for the probable English mistakes in my explanation since it is not my native language.. But thank you for reading it if you did ^^",
